WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.082 --> 00:00:02.060
(intrepid pop music)

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.470
- My name is Danny Tomsett.

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:06.450
I'm the CEO and founder of FaceMe,

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:08.660
and FaceMe is a company that has built

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.150
the world-leading digital human platform,

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:14.090
which is all about creating
an emotional connection

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:15.230
in a digital world.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:16.920
One of the challenges for customers,

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.970
particularly as they're
interacting more and more

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:21.787
on digital channels
and not with humans is,

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:23.707
"How do I know that you understand me?"

00:00:23.707 --> 00:00:25.947
"How do you personalize
an experience to me?"

00:00:25.947 --> 00:00:30.210
"How do we create better
man and machine interfaces,

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.780
because they're becoming such
a common part of our life?"

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.820
We've seen just this incredible response,

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.550
based on the fact that our face,

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:40.300
is probably the most universal interface

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.420
that's ever existed anyway.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.180
So, it's been really interesting

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:47.720
just learning around how
people enjoy conversation.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:50.630
How they actually...

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:53.774
create empathy themselves
for a digital human.

00:00:53.774 --> 00:00:55.040
(intrepid pop music)

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.530
We're a startup company.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.420
We provide this as a subscription,

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.960
and our whole vision is
around how making this

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.100
incredibly easy for any
organization to consume

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.820
and build experiences
using digital humans.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.430
So as a global company
with global customers,

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:11.530
you know Cloud is supporting that need.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:14.203
Both in the geographical sense,

00:01:14.203 --> 00:01:16.760
and IBM Cloud helps us with that.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.570
I believe that the interface
between man and machine

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:20.980
is gonna change dramatically.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.540
In the next five to ten years,

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:24.430
you're gonna see they're more humanized

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.150
and more personalized than ever before.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:27.490
That's what we're super excited about,

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:29.289
and that's our vision for the future.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:32.372
(intrepid pop music)

